---
description: Keep the product demo walkthrough synchronized with feature changes
alwaysApply: true
---

Whenever you add, modify, or remove a user-facing feature, update the existing demo walkthrough as part of the same task.

Inspect the existing demo documentation, recording scripts, narration, subtitles, fixtures, and role-based journeys before making changes. Reuse them rather than creating another walkthrough.

DEMO COVERAGE

Check whether the change affects:
- Platform Admin.
- Organization Admin.
- Campaign Organizer.
- Merchant.
- Supporter.
- Organization purchase and feature selection.
- Public website and campaign navigation.

Update only the affected journeys, while keeping the complete walkthrough coherent.

For optional features:
- Show how the organization enables the feature.
- Show any campaign-level configuration.
- Show the relevant user experience.
- Demonstrate the disabled state when important.

UPDATE THESE ARTIFACTS

Maintain the project's existing equivalents of:
- Demo scene checklist.
- Feature-to-scene coverage map.
- Narration script.
- Browser recording scripts.
- Demo fixtures.
- Expected results.

Use stable scene IDs so individual scenes can be re-recorded.

For each affected scene, record:
- Role and organization.
- Required feature settings.
- Starting state.
- Actions.
- Expected visible result.
- Narration.
- Dependencies on earlier scenes.

FEATURE CHANGE WORKFLOW

1. Implement the feature.
2. Verify its working behaviour and permissions.
3. Update relevant demo data without overwriting user data.
4. Update the walkthrough and narration.
5. Update and run affected recording scripts.
6. Re-record affected scenes when recording tools are available.
7. Reassemble the main video when clips or narration change.
8. Regenerate subtitle timings from the final narration/edit.
9. Review the resulting video for accuracy and continuity.

Do not regenerate the entire recording when isolated scenes can be replaced reliably.

If a changed scene affects later state, update or re-record dependent scenes too.

ACCURACY

- Demonstrate actual working interactions.
- Preserve all five role boundaries.
- Keep payments, AI previews, subscriptions, and voucher redemption clearly labelled where simulated.
- Do not describe unfinished functionality as working.
- Do not claim localStorage data works across devices.
- Keep credentials and private data out of recordings.

VIDEO FRESHNESS

Track:
- Last verified application commit or version.
- Recording date.
- Scenes affected by subsequent changes.
- Whether the final video is current or stale.

If recording, voice-over, or encoding tools are unavailable:
- Complete the walkthrough, narration, fixtures, and scripts.
- Mark affected clips and the final video as needing regeneration.
- State the exact blocker.
- Never claim the video was updated.

COMPLETION REPORT

At the end of each feature task, report:
- Feature implemented.
- Roles and demo scenes affected.
- Walkthrough/script updates completed.
- Checks performed.
- Video regenerated, or explicitly marked stale with the reason.

Do not upload, publish, or use paid voice-over services without authorization.

ARTIFACT LOCATIONS

The walkthrough lives in `together/demo-video/`. Do not start a second one.

- Scene checklist, fixtures, actions, and expected results: `together/demo-video/scripts/scenes.mjs` (stable `id`s; `record: false` scenes are off-camera fixtures).
- Narration: `together/demo-video/narration/script.md`. One non-heading line is one subtitle cue. `{shown|spoken}` when the subtitle and speech differ.
- Timed script from the last assembly: `together/demo-video/narration/scene-timings.md`.
- Feature-to-scene coverage and unfinished behaviour: `together/demo-video/FEATURE-STATUS.md`.
- Browser recording, local voice, and assembly: `together/demo-video/scripts/record.mjs`, `narrate.mjs`, `assemble.mjs`.
- Video freshness: the "Video freshness" section in `together/demo-video/README.md`.
- Rendered video, chapter clips, and subtitles (not committed): `together/demo-video/output/`.

Recording uses a throwaway Chrome profile. Never read or write the user's normal browser storage.

Rebuild only what changed: `node narrate.mjs`, then `DRY=1 FROM=<sceneId>` to check a scene, then a captured run of the affected scenes, then `node assemble.mjs`. Replace whole-video capture only when later scenes depend on new state that checkpoints cannot resume.
